                <pb facs="0806" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg718"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay informs Mr. McCormick that the British steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ettrick Dale</hi> will be dispatched to Korsakov by the Japanese Government
                    to withdraw their subjects, and that the same will leave Hakodate about April
                    28. Instructs him to request the Russian <pb facs="0807" n="719" xml:id="pg719"
                    /> Government to telegraph this information to the Russian authorities at
                    Korsakov; to inform the Japanese consulate at Korsakov, through the commercial
                    agent at Vladivostok, that, as far as possible, the Japanese residents in
                    Saghalien should be gathered before the arrival of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ettrick Dale</hi>, which, in addition to the passengers, will be able to
                    take away a large amount of freight.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
